{"title":"2007 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle is inscribed in an equilateral triangle whose side\nlength is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then another circle is inscribed externally\ntangent to the first circle but inside the triangle as shown.\nAnd then another, and another. If this process continues\nforever what is the total area of all the circles? Express\nyour answer as an exact multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> (and not as a\ndecimal approximation).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/f/8af6a485cf6e58a89645057e34404328fd5cbaa7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] path T=polygon(3); draw(unitcircle,black); draw(scale(2)*T,black); draw(shift(2/sqrt(3),-2/3)*scale(1/3)*unitcircle,black); draw(shift(2/sqrt(3)/3,-2/9)*shift(2/sqrt(3),-2/3)*scale(1/9)*unitcircle,black); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"218\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be the equilateral triangle and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/6/f468920603bf6bb9fc352c0b775c4c350b2dd9a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1B_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> be the internal common tangent of the two largest circles, with the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/243af6fad28c15abb3e11996374ba60e745bf543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> laying on the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the point of tangency of the two circles.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2f5d57528aa7eeb9d5080cb5c25b4b06192862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> be the inscribed circle's radius, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> being its center and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> being the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bfc6159e268a0f5d736eca73477c99a13209da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> be the triangle's altitude. We can calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2f5d57528aa7eeb9d5080cb5c25b4b06192862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> using Pythagoras' Theorem:\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62fe76846cbedd71eeea21e84d85cf8245b66baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM^2 = BO^2 - BM^2$\" width=\"165\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/7/8377f9d0ba46c11197a474a5e491e6b37fd24ff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM^2 = \\left(\\frac{2}{3} \\times BH \\right)^2 - \\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\times AB \\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"284\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/b/40bd511ac85652033a40a456d10f6cfaf08bec16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM^2 = \\left( \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{3} \\right)^2 - 1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"176\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/8938f3d6018aa79f2f17cf52587bc68a8d3cf15a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM = \\frac{\\sqrt3}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"85\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a2d84945169e46661f99b0c6615480056765cc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow OM = \\frac{BH}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"115\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\nFrom there we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/f/48ffb502755b67846b22edbde6a9476925367964.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BL = OM = \\frac{BH}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"143\" height=\"37\" />. This means the scale factor of the similar triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c70ffa349087c7abbd95cfc3bb36f41056cd2e27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1B_1B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b8229eaa7fcc15afd947a18d7c921214b5d94748.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> (because the ratio of their altitudes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/4532333f06364eb7662c0ab58ba0c5dcf0a19fb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BL}{BH}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"33\" height=\"37\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> .) \n</p><p>Since the smaller circle is inscribed in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c70ffa349087c7abbd95cfc3bb36f41056cd2e27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1B_1B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />, its radius is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/0649ccc04f038e56b5c7455c7c61a2b9978dbeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{OM}{3} = \\frac{\\sqrt3}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"89\" height=\"41\" /> . Repeating this trend infinitely and summing all the areas gives us: \n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/6/8d6a4f07c69447b0dce99c022d2e03894ae2e80d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Area = \\pi \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{3}\\right)^2 + \\pi \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{9}\\right)^2 + \\pi \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{27}\\right)^2 +\\pi \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{81}\\right)^2 + ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"478\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/4/0546d301e30880a11fe1318941451a42661fc632.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Area = \\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{3^3} + \\frac{1}{3^5} + \\frac{1}{3^7} + ... \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"280\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><br />\nWe have the geometric progression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302d303ba17879eff7b108e0beb88659440111f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_n = \\frac{1}{3^{2n-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"91\" height=\"37\" /> with a scale factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> and a common ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594c8b267069448b58fe77ad60497eb30f763a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />&#160;:\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7157944d8381c92c42e2e7c3cc2b46ab042a05a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Area = \\pi \\times \\frac{\\frac{1}{3}}{1 - \\frac{1}{9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"142\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2b59af76a08bce29de9963c003c48ca9732d44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Area = \\frac{3}{8} \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"2007 UNCO Math Contest II\">2007 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2007 UNCO Math Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 UNCO Math Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://uncmathcontest.wordpress.com/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2007 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2007 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_Northern_Colorado_Math_Contest\" title=\"University of Northern Colorado Math Contest\"> All UNCO Math Contest Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017213945\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 238/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1409/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 96/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6914/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.258      1 Template:UNCO_Math_Contest_box\n100.00%    7.258      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13612:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017213945 and revision id 90057. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}